        "original_id": "bcef5e86-0fa7-50b4-9ac3-73bb66b3d2f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ed Wood, Fernand Rivers, Bela Lugosi, Dolores Fuller\n- Works: Glen or Glenda\n- Roles: filmmaker, actor, writer, producer, director, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Fernand Rivers was born as François Large on 6 September 1879 in Saint-Lager and became a French actor, screenwriter, film producer, and director.\n- Ed Wood, born Edward Davis Wood Jr. on October 10, 1924, was an American filmmaker, actor, writer, producer, and director.\n- Glen or Glenda is a 1953 American drama film written, directed by, and starring Ed Wood, who was credited in the starring role as Daniel Davis.\n- Glen or Glenda features Bela Lugosi and Ed Wood's then-girlfriend Dolores Fuller.\n- Fernand Rivers died on 12 September 1960.\n- Ed Wood died on December 10, 1978.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9361f956-4c92-55e6-a2a1-44fcc88b17bb",
        "text": "Page: Ed Wood. Sentence: Edward Davis Wood Jr. (October 10, 1924 – December 10, 1978) was an American filmmaker, actor, writer, producer, and director.\nPage: Fernand Rivers. Sentence: Fernand Rivers (born François Large, 6 September 1879, Saint-Lager - 12 September 1960) was a French actor, screenwriter, film producer and director.\nPage: Glen or Glenda. Sentence: Glen or Glenda is a 1953 American drama film written, directed by and starring Ed Wood (credited in his starring role as \"Daniel Davis\"), and featuring Bela Lugosi and Wood's then-girlfriend Dolores Fuller.",
